WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.748
One input changes. Now your AI agent has

2
00:00:03.788 --> 00:00:05.876
to work out what that broke.

3
00:00:06.426 --> 00:00:08.464
Today, it has two options.

4
00:00:09.014 --> 00:00:11.494
Re-read everything. Accurate,

5
00:00:11.534 --> 00:00:12.955
but you pay for every token,

6
00:00:12.995 --> 00:00:14.316
every time.

7
00:00:14.866 --> 00:00:17.527
Or search for what looks related.

8
00:00:17.677 --> 00:00:20.402
Cheap, but blind to what matters.

9
00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:23.963
Agents build reports on their own earlier

10
00:00:24.003 --> 00:00:27.243
work, so every number quietly depends on

11
00:00:27.283 --> 00:00:28.623
inputs underneath.

12
00:00:28.873 --> 00:00:30.153
Correct one exchange rate,

13
00:00:30.193 --> 00:00:32.522
and some of those numbers are now wrong.

14
00:00:32.772 --> 00:00:34.712
But a total can depend on that rate

15
00:00:34.752 --> 00:00:36.480
without ever mentioning it.

16
00:00:36.730 --> 00:00:39.349
Similar words are not the same as real

17
00:00:39.389 --> 00:00:40.450
dependencies.

18
00:00:41.650 --> 00:00:43.943
ProofFlow is a context layer that follows

19
00:00:43.983 --> 00:00:46.076
structure instead of guessing.

20
00:00:46.326 --> 00:00:48.256
Every number keeps its receipts:

21
00:00:48.346 --> 00:00:50.686
exactly which inputs, and which tool,

22
00:00:50.726 --> 00:00:51.726
made it.

23
00:00:51.836 --> 00:00:53.296
So when something changes,

24
00:00:53.336 --> 00:00:55.346
the agent gets exactly what broke.

25
00:00:55.516 --> 00:00:56.565
Nothing more.

26
00:00:58.550 --> 00:01:00.806
An input, like the exchange rate,

27
00:01:00.876 --> 00:01:02.507
is saved as a version.

28
00:01:02.757 --> 00:01:05.394
A tool reads it, and leaves a receipt.

29
00:01:05.644 --> 00:01:07.634
The receipt points to its result,

30
00:01:07.784 --> 00:01:10.004
and each number in a report points to that

31
00:01:10.044 --> 00:01:11.044
result.

32
00:01:11.471 --> 00:01:13.093
Now, correct the rate.

33
00:01:13.543 --> 00:01:15.493
The change travels up those links.

34
00:01:15.923 --> 00:01:17.913
Both revenue figures are withheld,

35
00:01:18.103 --> 00:01:19.613
never shown stale.

36
00:01:19.863 --> 00:01:21.483
Support never read the rate,

37
00:01:21.523 --> 00:01:24.353
so it stays current, and is reused.

38
00:01:24.603 --> 00:01:27.806
Refresh re-runs only the affected steps.

39
00:01:29.550 --> 00:01:32.027
This is ProofFlow, live today.

40
00:01:32.277 --> 00:01:34.067
Upload orders as a CSV,

41
00:01:34.437 --> 00:01:37.121
preview them, and create two reports.

42
00:01:37.371 --> 00:01:38.901
Publish a corrected rate.

43
00:01:39.531 --> 00:01:41.161
Affected figures are withheld,

44
00:01:41.371 --> 00:01:43.390
and the graph shows exactly why.

45
00:01:43.640 --> 00:01:45.203
Refresh brings them current.

46
00:01:45.933 --> 00:01:48.113
A checked report can only be copied while

47
00:01:48.153 --> 00:01:49.794
every figure is current.

48
00:01:50.044 --> 00:01:52.554
Agents get the same workflow through MCP.

49
00:01:52.944 --> 00:01:55.012
Six tools, one download.

50
00:01:56.550 --> 00:01:57.936
Under the hood, it's small,

51
00:01:57.976 --> 00:01:59.319
and strict.

52
00:01:59.769 --> 00:02:01.435
At the center is the runtime.

53
00:02:01.965 --> 00:02:04.145
Every tool run produces an immutable

54
00:02:04.185 --> 00:02:06.107
result, and a receipt.

55
00:02:06.357 --> 00:02:08.997
Content goes into a store that verifies

56
00:02:09.037 --> 00:02:10.432
every hash.

57
00:02:10.682 --> 00:02:12.665
Relationships go into HydraDB,

58
00:02:12.705 --> 00:02:14.619
as a lineage graph.

59
00:02:14.869 --> 00:02:16.379
When a correction arrives,

60
00:02:16.509 --> 00:02:18.709
HydraDB walks that graph natively,

61
00:02:18.749 --> 00:02:20.920
to find everything downstream.

62
00:02:21.170 --> 00:02:23.630
That walk becomes the agent's context.

63
00:02:23.900 --> 00:02:25.390
Traverse the structure.

64
00:02:25.660 --> 00:02:26.718
Skip the re-read.

65
00:02:26.968 --> 00:02:29.477
The runtime re-runs stale steps in order,

66
00:02:29.827 --> 00:02:31.217
reuses what's current,

67
00:02:31.427 --> 00:02:33.144
and records new receipts.

68
00:02:33.394 --> 00:02:34.804
If evidence is missing,

69
00:02:34.914 --> 00:02:36.984
it fails closed. No fallback.

70
00:02:37.274 --> 00:02:38.274
No guess.

71
00:02:38.336 --> 00:02:40.766
Agents reach it through a browser app,

72
00:02:40.956 --> 00:02:43.806
a Python API, or an MCP server,

73
00:02:43.936 --> 00:02:46.106
choosing plans from typed tools,

74
00:02:46.496 --> 00:02:48.120
never arbitrary code.

75
00:02:56.450 --> 00:02:58.626
So how does it compare to today's

76
00:02:58.666 --> 00:02:59.722
approaches?

77
00:03:00.172 --> 00:03:02.972
We froze one study. Forty-eight real model

78
00:03:03.012 --> 00:03:05.677
calls, the same task for every method.

79
00:03:05.927 --> 00:03:07.966
Re-reading everything got all thirty-two

80
00:03:08.006 --> 00:03:09.486
reports right, for three dollars

81
00:03:09.526 --> 00:03:10.719
seventy-four.

82
00:03:10.969 --> 00:03:12.729
ProofFlow also got thirty-two of

83
00:03:12.769 --> 00:03:14.781
thirty-two, with a hundred forty-two

84
00:03:14.821 --> 00:03:16.609
thousand fewer input tokens,

85
00:03:16.649 --> 00:03:18.359
for a dollar thirty-eight.

86
00:03:18.769 --> 00:03:20.784
Sixty-three percent less.

87
00:03:21.034 --> 00:03:22.801
Vector search cost the same as ProofFlow,

88
00:03:22.841 --> 00:03:25.461
and got five right. Keyword search,

89
00:03:25.501 --> 00:03:28.497
twenty-five. Hybrid, twenty-eight.

90
00:03:28.747 --> 00:03:30.478
On a separate retail benchmark,

91
00:03:30.518 --> 00:03:31.698
thirty-eight of thirty-eight,

92
00:03:31.738 --> 00:03:33.878
with sixty-nine percent fewer evidence

93
00:03:33.918 --> 00:03:34.918
tokens.

94
00:03:35.109 --> 00:03:37.103
A plain dependency walk over the same

95
00:03:37.143 --> 00:03:40.103
links ties it. The win is recording the

96
00:03:40.143 --> 00:03:41.143
structure.

97
00:03:42.450 --> 00:03:43.478
ProofFlow.

98
00:03:43.728 --> 00:03:45.227
Full-context accuracy,

99
00:03:45.267 --> 00:03:47.562
at vector-search cost.

100
00:03:47.812 --> 00:03:49.475
Built for teams whose agents produce

101
00:03:49.515 --> 00:03:51.265
numbers people act on:

102
00:03:51.635 --> 00:03:54.205
finance, revenue, analytics.

103
00:03:54.915 --> 00:03:57.421
Add it to any agent through MCP.

104
00:03:57.671 --> 00:04:00.914
Try it live. Every number shown is in the

105
00:04:00.954 --> 00:04:02.234
public evidence.
